+// the three GPU stage boundaries against an independent double-precision
+// oracle written in this file (not sharing a conversion routine with the
+// kernel under test -- see f16_bits_to_f32/f32_to_f16_bits below). T1b checks
+// the AVX2 kernel against the scalar reference (skipped on a host without
+// AVX2). T1c predicts the on-card half-accumulation divergence and records
+// it as a property; it does not gate pass/fail.
+//
+// Red-first (CLAUDE.md, this patch's HARD RULE): before moe_cpu_expert.cpp's
+// dequant_weight() indexed the low/high nibble as (k&1)==0 -> low, this test
+// was run against a build with the two branches of that ternary swapped
+// (spec §8's red case 1, the nibble-order flip). T1a failed by ~10x the bound
+// (achieved max relative error was O(1), not O(2^-18)) -- see this patch's
+// report for the verbatim red run. Reverting the flip and rebuilding is what
+// makes this test green; that is the change this patch actually contains.
